## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design end-to-end privacy-preserving data pipelines with real-time orchestration, a combination of managed ML endpoints, and robust governance controls.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven ingestion (S3, EventBridge/Step Functions)
- Privacy: PII redaction, customerIdHash, encryption at rest/transit, retention policies
- Observability: Dead-letter queues, retry logic with exponential backoff, CloudWatch metrics
- Data governance: Cross-region replication, IAM least-privilege access, compliance requirements

## Code Example
```python
# State Machine Definition (Amazon States Language)
{
  "StartAt": "InvokeSageMaker",
  "States": {
    "InvokeSageMaker": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "arn:aws:lambda:us-east-1:123456789012:function:classifyChat",
        "Payload": { "S3Bucket."S.$": "$.bucket", "S3Key."S.$": "$.key" }
      },
      "Next": "RedactPII"
    },
    "RedactPII": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "arn:aws:lambda:us-east-1:123456789012:function:redactPII",
        "Payload": { "transcript.$": "$.transcript", "threadId.$": "$.threadId" }
      },
      "Next": "UpsertDynamoDB"
    },
    "UpsertDynamoDB": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::dynamodb:putItem",
      "Parameters": {
        "TableName": "ChatIndex",
        "Item": {
          "threadId": { "S.$": "$.threadId" },
          "customerIdHash": { "S.$": "$.customerIdHash" },
          "topIntents": { "L.$": "$.intents" },
          "sentiment": { "S.$": "$.sentiment" },
          "retentionDate": { "S.$": "$.retentionDate" }
        }
      },
      "End": true
    }
  }
}
```

## Architecture Diagram
S3 (upload) → EventBridge → Step Functions → SageMaker (ML) → Lambda (PII) → S3 (anonymized) → DynamoDB (index)
